%%{init: {'theme': 'base', 'themeVariables': {'fontFamily': 'Arial', 'fontSize': '17px', 'primaryColor': '#eef4ff', 'primaryTextColor': '#172033', 'primaryBorderColor': '#6487bc', 'lineColor': '#6487bc'}, 'flowchart': {'nodeSpacing': 30, 'rankSpacing': 28, 'padding': 16, 'wrappingWidth': 600}}}%%
flowchart TD
    A["1. Define the contract<br/>What must be true when push returns?<br/>Which failures must the record survive?"]
    A --> B["2. Direct append<br/>Every caller opens, appends, and closes the file.<br/>What breaks when two threads write concurrently?"]
    B --> C["3. Serialize with a mutex<br/>Which operations belong inside the lock?<br/>Does closing the file guarantee durability?"]
    C --> D["4. Persist each record<br/>Explain flush versus fsync.<br/>When exactly may push return successfully?"]
    D --> E["5. Frame the records<br/>How do you distinguish arbitrary byte payloads?<br/>How do you handle a short write?"]
    E --> F["6. Recover after a crash<br/>What if the file ends halfway through a record?<br/>What can a checksum detect—and what can it not guarantee?"]
    F --> G["7. Identify the performance bottleneck<br/>Every push holds the mutex through fsync.<br/>What happens with thousands of callers?"]
    G --> H["8. Introduce group commit<br/>How can one fsync serve multiple callers?<br/>Design a shared queue and one background writer."]
    H --> I["9. Separate queue coordination from disk I/O<br/>Can callers enqueue while the writer syncs?<br/>Which shared state still requires the mutex?"]
    I --> J["10. Acknowledge the correct records<br/>Assign a sequence number to each accepted record.<br/>Syncing 1–100 while 101 arrives: who may return?"]
    J --> K["11. Coordinate waiting callers<br/>How does a condition variable work?<br/>Why must callers recheck a predicate after waking?"]
    K --> L["12. Bound batching latency<br/>What if traffic stops below the size threshold?<br/>When does the batch deadline start?"]
    L --> M["13. Apply backpressure<br/>What if producers outrun the disk?<br/>Do queued and in-flight bytes both count?"]
    M --> N["14. Handle permanent failure<br/>fsync fails: what state changes?<br/>How do durability and capacity waiters escape?"]
    N --> O["15. Explain uncertain outcomes<br/>Can a failed push still leave a valid record?<br/>What happens if the caller retries?"]
    O --> P["16. Shut down safely<br/>close races with push: which records are accepted?<br/>How do you drain them without deadlocking?"]
    P --> Q["17. Validate the guarantees<br/>Inject short writes, sync failures, and crashes.<br/>Why does killing a process not simulate power loss?"]
    Q --> R["18. Extend the API<br/>If push returns before durability,<br/>how can callers await a durable acknowledgment?"]
    R --> S["19. Rotate files safely<br/>How do you coordinate queued records, file switches,<br/>directory syncs, recovery, and acknowledgments?"]
